### 3.3 Electrical and Chemical Signalling

Signals are transmitted along neuronal axons by **action potentials**. At specialized
contacts called **synapses**, neurotransmitters are released, bind to receptor
molecules on target neurons, and alter the membrane potential.

This process requires energy from oxygen and metabolites supplied by the vascular
system. Measurements of increased energy consumption and blood flow in active brain
regions provide the basis for **fMRI**.

---

## 4. Localization of Function: Penfield and the Homunculus

### 4.1 Wilder Penfield (1891-1976)

Canadian neurosurgeon who sought better ways of mapping the cerebral cortex to
minimize damage during surgery.

~~~voxi
CANVAS 660 260 #0f1117
-- Method diagram
RECT 20 10 300 240 1 #1a1a3a 8
TEXT 36 24 "PENFIELD'S METHOD" 13 2 #e040fb bold

-- Step boxes
RECT 36 48 268 36 2 #1a2a4a 6
TEXT 46 56 "1. Expose cortex during surgery" 10 3 #6c8cff
RECT 36 92 268 36 2 #1a2a4a 6
TEXT 46 100 "2. Apply weak electrical currents" 10 3 #6c8cff
RECT 36 136 268 36 2 #1a2a4a 6
TEXT 46 144 "3. Patient reports sensations" 10 3 #6c8cff
RECT 36 180 268 36 2 #1a2a4a 6
TEXT 46 188 "4. Map stimulation -> sensation" 10 3 #6c8cff
TEXT 36 228 "Patient is AWAKE throughout" 9 2 #ef9a9a

-- Result: Homunculus diagram (simplified)
RECT 340 10 300 240 1 #0f1a2a 8
TEXT 356 24 "THE HOMUNCULUS" 13 2 #1e88e5 bold

-- Simplified body map (top to bottom = medial to lateral)
RECT 362 50 18 14 2 #2e7d32 3
TEXT 384 52 "Feet/Legs" 9 3 #81c784
TEXT 500 52 "(top of brain)" 8 3 #5a5a6a

RECT 362 70 18 14 2 #1e88e5 3
TEXT 384 72 "Trunk" 9 3 #90caf9

RECT 362 90 26 18 2 #fdd835 3
TEXT 392 92 "Arms" 9 3 #d4c87a

RECT 362 114 50 28 2 #ff9800 3
TEXT 416 120 "Hands" 9 3 #ffb74d
TEXT 500 120 "(large area!)" 8 3 #5a5a6a

RECT 362 148 56 34 2 #e53935 3
TEXT 422 158 "Face/Lips" 9 3 #ef9a9a
TEXT 500 158 "(largest area!)" 8 3 #5a5a6a

RECT 362 188 24 16 2 #ab47bc 3
TEXT 390 190 "Tongue" 9 3 #ce93d8
TEXT 500 190 "(side of brain)" 8 3 #5a5a6a

TEXT 362 218 "More sensitive body parts =" 9 2 #8888a0
TEXT 362 234 "larger cortical representation" 9 2 #fdd835
~~~

Body parts with greater sensory sensitivity (hands, face, lips) have
**disproportionately larger** cortical representation. Stimulation near the top
of the brain produces sensations in feet and legs; stimulation on the side produces
sensations in face and lips.

