### 5.1 Prefrontal Cortex: Comparative Anatomy

Early scientists believed frontal lobes were critical for controlling behaviour.
Modern research (Semendeferi et al.) shows:

~~~chart bar
"Prefrontal Cortex % of Total" = Dog:7 Cat:4 Monkey:10 Apes:20 Humans:30
colors = #8888a0 #8888a0 #8888a0 #ff9800 #6c8cff
~~~

> [!note] Key Insight
> Humans are distinctive because of their **relatively large brains overall**,
> not because of disproportionately large prefrontal cortices. Proportional size
> of frontal lobes in humans (~35%) is similar to great apes.

