### 7.2 Diaschisis — Critical Concept for Lesion Studies

> [!warning] Diaschisis
> If one brain area is lesioned, other **connected** areas may also stop
> functioning normally due to loss of input. This can lead to wrongly attributing
> the lost functionality to the lesioned area rather than a downstream area.

~~~graph directed
[Lesioned Area] --> [Connected Area A]
[Lesioned Area] --> [Connected Area B]
[Connected Area A] --> [Downstream Function]
[Connected Area B] --> [Downstream Function]
colors = #e53935 #ff9800 #ff9800 #fdd835
~~~

Damage to cortical areas can also damage nearby fibre tracts, disrupting more
distant areas. Despite these limitations, lesion studies remain highly informative,
especially with modern MRI that allows precise localization of lesions.

### 7.3 Pharmacological Perturbations

~~~voxi
CANVAS 660 110 #0f1117
-- Agonist
RECT 20 10 300 90 1 #0f2a1a 8
TEXT 36 24 "AGONIST" 14 2 #43a047 bold
TEXT 36 46 "Activates receptors like" 10 2 #81c784
TEXT 36 62 "natural neurotransmitters" 10 2 #81c784
TEXT 36 82 "Example: nicotine" 9 2 #8888a0

-- Antagonist
RECT 340 10 300 90 1 #2a0f0f 8
TEXT 356 24 "ANTAGONIST" 14 2 #e53935 bold
TEXT 356 46 "Blocks receptors," 10 2 #ef9a9a
TEXT 356 62 "prevents activation" 10 2 #ef9a9a
TEXT 356 82 "Example: haloperidol" 9 2 #8888a0
~~~

**Dopamine system** plays a major role in reward evaluation. Cocaine addicts show
impaired reward evaluation via changes in the dopamine system. **Drug tolerance**
refers to needing increasing amounts to achieve the same pharmacological effect.

---

## 8. Neuroimaging Genomics

**Polymorphisms:** Variations in a gene or segment of DNA that can be associated
with greater risk of neurological and psychiatric disorders.

~~~voxi
