## 10. Multimethodological Synthesis

The most effective cognitive neuroscience research **combines multiple methods**
both within and across studies. This holds the promise for the deepest understanding
of neural processes underlying cognition.

~~~graph directed
[EEG] --> [Temporal Info]
[fMRI] --> [Spatial Info]
[TMS] --> [Causal Evidence]
[Lesion Studies] --> [Causal Evidence]
[Temporal Info] --> [Integrated Model]
[Spatial Info] --> [Integrated Model]
[Causal Evidence] --> [Integrated Model]
colors = #43a047 #1e88e5 #ff9800 #e53935 #fdd835 #fdd835 #fdd835 #e040fb
~~~

> [!note] Exam Tip: "What is the advantage of using multiple methods?"
> **Convergence** — agreeing results increase confidence.
> **Complementarity** — different methods reveal different aspects of the same
> phenomenon that no single method can capture alone.

